Z||000009||LVMY88||10-21-2001||10:08 AM||||How did the dinner go?<P><BR>Sorry we couldn't be there but on Saturdays this time of year we have lot's of soccer. Tarrah had a soccer tournament in Sutton NH all day. Out of 6 qualifying teams, Tarrah's team came in second! They had to play three games right in a row, with only a five minute break between them to change fields.<BR>They won the first game 4-0 over kersarge. They won the second game against Belmont 5-1. The girls were exhausted by the time they played the third game against Hartland VT, and lost 2-0. <BR>That is the best the Plainfield girls soccer team has ever done. I don't think it is coincidence that this just so happens to be the first year that Tarrah has been on this team as she is now in 7th grade.<P><BR>While I was in Sutton with Tarrah and her team, Steve took Jordan to his final game at the Plainfield school. Jordan and his team also came in second out of 4 qualifying teams. Jordan was the goalie for three out of the four periods. He allowed only one goal out of 16 on goal shots, so Jordan was awesome as goalie!<P><BR>Soccer rules in this house   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P><BR>Marian<P><BR>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Marianssmallsig.jpg">  <p>[This message has been edited by LVMY88 (edited 10-22-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000010||88CoupeV6||10-21-2001||06:25 PM||||LVMY88, Sorry you guys couldn't make it. We had a good time. There were only 6 of us. Me & Jaime, Eric, Jim Lund, Ray, and Jeong Kim. Have Steve e-mail me with a date, place, and time for next month. Make it earlier so Phil Gwen can make it. They have to get home for the cat.||||reg||7
